"Collects all image nodes from the document tree and tracks them in "
"self.images dictionary for later copying to the output directory."
msgstr ""

#: of typsphinx.builder.TypstBuilder.post_process_images:6
msgid ""
"For a `*`-glob image URI (e.g. ``.. figure:: _static/foo.*``), Sphinx's "
"read-phase ImageCollector leaves ``node[\"uri\"]`` as the literal, "
"unresolved glob string and instead records the concrete on-disk "
"candidates in ``node[\"candidates\"]`` keyed by mimetype -- resolving "
"that to one concrete file is the builder's responsibility (mirrors "
"``sphinx.builders.Builder.post_process_images``, as done by the "
"HTML/LaTeX builders via their own ``supported_image_types``). This picks "
"the best Typst-embeddable candidate and rewrites ``node[\"uri\"]`` to the"
" resolved path, so both the translator's ``visit_image`` (emits the path "
"into the ``.typ``) and ``copy_image_files()`` (copies the file) see the "
"concrete file."
